# Drafted by Gemini (R16 clock), edited.

~ midnight_swarm
cutscene sk_floor_boils
Narrator: The twelfth bell has barely died in the fog when the coarse wool blanket on the well-side bier begins to sag and ripple. A thick, sweet stench of bad cider and wet earth rises from the planks.
cutscene sk_floor_boils_2
Narrator: Whatever poor soul lay under that cloth has given up being a neighbour. With a dry, papery rustle like a sack of autumn leaves split open, ten thousand shiny brown backs boil out onto the cobbles.
cutscene end
* Stand our ground and fight it -> fight
* Run for the Green Queen and bar the door -> run

~ fight
approve rook_coldwake +2 lucan_houndstooth +2: You stood your ground against the midnight swarm
Narrator: You draw your steel against a tide of clicking legs that has no face to strike and no heart to pierce.
combat sk_midnight_swarm

~ run
approve rook_coldwake -2 lucan_houndstooth -2 silas_vane +1: You barred yourselves inside while the swarm passed
Narrator: You slam the heavy oak behind you and drop the iron bar into its brackets. Through the leaded glass, you watch the long, dark ribbon of legs carry the empty blanket away toward the north-west hills.
